'''Tasi Lowa''' was a [[Zygerrian]] [[Jedi]] of the [[Jedi Order]] who lived during the [[High Republic Era]]. She was the [[Padawan]] of [[Jedi Knight]] [[Yord Fandar]]. Lowa and Fandar visited the [[Trade Federation]] [[WD-2550 Whydah-class Yield Conveyer|freighter]] ''[[Fallon]]'' to find the [[meknek]] [[Verosha Aniseya|Verosha "Osha" Aniseya]], who was incriminated for the [[Indara's murder|murder]] of [[Jedi Master]] [[Indara]] by her [[twin]] [[Gender|sister]], [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae-ho "Mae" Aniseya]]. The Zygerrian [[Mission to arrest Osha Aniseya|questioned]] Osha, who claimed she was innocent, but the two [[Jedi]] apprehended the meknek and delivered her to the [[Galactic Republic]] [[DTE-CSA-17 Calaboose prison ship|prison ship]] ''[[Palwick]]''.

==Biography==
{{Quote|The suspect matched your description.''"<br />"''You think that I killed her?''"<br />"''Where were you last night?''"<br />"''On this freighter. In this room.|Tasi Lowa questions Verosha Aniseya|<ref name="Lost / Found" />}}
The [[Force-sensitive]]<ref name="Lost / Found" /> [[Zygerrian]]<ref name="L/F Trivia" /> Tasi Lowa was a [[Jedi]] of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="Lost / Found" /> By [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> she<ref name="Lost / Found AD" /> was the [[Padawan]] of [[Jedi Knight]] [[Yord Fandar]] and was stationed at the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on<ref name="Databank" /> the [[capital]] planet<ref name="Lost / Found AD" /> [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Databank" /> In that [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="Date" /> after [[Jedi Master]] [[Indara]] was [[Indara's murder|murdered]] by the [[The Force|Force]]-sensitive [[assassin]]<ref name="Lost / Found" /> [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae-ho "Mae" Aniseya]]<ref name="Destiny">{{Acolyte|Destiny (The Acolyte)}}</ref> on [[Ueda]], Lowa [[Mission to arrest Osha Aniseya|accompanied]] Fandar to the [[Trade Federation]] [[WD-2550 Whydah-class Yield Conveyer|freighter]]<ref name="Lost / Found" /> ''[[Fallon]]''<ref name="Databank Fallon">{{Databank|fallon-freighter|Fallon freighter}}</ref> to apprehend the [[meknek]]<ref name="Lost / Found" /> [[Verosha Aniseya|Verosha "Osha" Aniseya]]<ref name="Destiny" />&mdash;a former Jedi Padawan to Master [[Sol]] and Mae's [[twin]] [[Gender|sister]]&mdash;who had been incriminated for the crime. The two Jedi landed on the [[freighter]] in a [[Jedi Vector]] and made their way to the [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]], where Fandar introduced himself and Lowa before asking the [[Neimoidian]] [[captain]] [[Blex]] about Osha. Although the captain denied having mekneks aboard, an [[Queya|officer]] revealed Osha's location.<ref name="Lost / Found" />

[[File:FandarLowaQuestionOsha-LostFound.png|thumb|left|300px|Fandar and Lowa question Osha in her quarters.]]
When Fandar met Osha in her quarters, Lowa entered, conversing with the former Jedi about her current job before questioning when she had joined the Order. Lowa noted that Osha's age had been a concern about her admittance to the Order, while Fandar brought up the [[Death|loss]] of Osha's family shortly before her entry. Osha asked why the Jedi were there, and Lowa informed her of the murder on Ueda by a suspect matching her description. When Osha protested the idea that she had killed Indara, Lowa asked her where she had been the previous [[Standard day|night]], and the meknek claimed she had been aboard the freighter.<ref name="Lost / Found" />

At Fandar's request, Lowa stepped out of the room, returning a moment later with the [[Bartender|barkeep]]<ref name="Lost / Found" /> [[Cabuck]],<ref name="Databank Lomi Usqi">{{Databank|lomi-usqi-noodle-shop|Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop}}</ref> who had witnessed the murder. The barkeep identified Osha as the murderer, and the two Jedi subsequently apprehended the meknek. As the Jedi escorted her to a the [[DTE-CSA-17 Calaboose prison ship|prison transport]]<ref name="Lost / Found" /> ''[[Palwick]]'',<ref name="Databank Palwick">{{Databank|palwick-prison-ship|Palwick prison ship}}</ref> which was to take her back to Coruscant, Lowa powered down Osha's [[PIP droid|droid]], [[Pip]], informing her of what her fate would be. Lowa handed the meknek's belongings to a [[Unidentified droid warden|droid warden]], who took Osha aboard, and the [[transport]] departed. The Jedi returned to Coruscant themselves, although Osha never arrived, the [[prison ship]] having crashed after the other [[prisoner]]s [[Prisoner mutiny on the Palwick|attempted]] to escape.<ref name="Lost / Found" />

Lowa did not accompany her Master to [[Khofar]], where he lost his life in a [[Mission to Khofar|battle]] with the [[Sith Lord]] known as [[The Stranger]].<ref name="Night">{{Acolyte|Night}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|So how long have you been a meknek?''"<br />"''Since I left the Order. So&hellip; six years.''"<br />"''Dangerous job.''"<br />"''It has its perks.|Tasi Lowa and Osha Aniseya|<ref name="Lost / Found" />}}
[[File:TasiLowa-YIR2024.png|thumb|250px|right|Tasi Lowa had brown hair and purple eyes.]]
Lowa had [[Color|brown]] hair, purple [[eye]]s, and light skin.<ref name="Lost / Found" /> As a Padawan, she was studious.<ref name="Databank" /> While questioning Osha, the Zygerrian<ref name="Lost / Found" /> gazed staunchly<ref name="Lost / Found AD" /> at the meknek, whose career Lowa knew to be dangerous.<ref name="Lost / Found" /> She stood at a height of 1.6 [[meter]]s.<ref name="Databank" />

==Powers and abilities==
As a Jedi of the Jedi Order, Lowa was a Force-sensitive [[Jedi training|trained]] to [[Force power|wield]] [[the Force]].<ref name="Lost / Found" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|A major concern about admitting you to the Order was your age.|Lowa reads off her datapad while questioning Osha|<ref name="Lost / Found" />}}
Lowa [[Clothing|wore]] a set of [[Jedi apparel]] that consisted of a white [[cape]] over a white and gold tunic. The Zygerrian also wore a brown [[belt]] over a green sash, as well as brown [[boot]]s. She had several gold bands that tied back her hair. While questioning Osha Aniseya, Lowa carried a [[datapad]].<ref name="Lost / Found" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Oh, I got a Zygerrian in live-action, which that was one of my things. I was like, 'I've got to get a Zygerrian.' The poor makeup department. Let me tell you what I put them through.|Leslye Headland|<ref name="Collider">{{WebCite|url=https://collider.com/the-acolyte-zygerrian-practical-effects-leslye-headland-comments|text='The Acolyte' Will Use Practical Effects for the Zygerrians Says Showrunner|author=Diego Peralta|date=2023-04-14|work=[[Wikipedia:Collider (website)|Collider]]|quote=Oh, I got a Zygerrian in live-action, which that was one of my things. I was like, 'I've got to get a Zygerrian.' The poor makeup department. Let me tell you what I put them through. She's a blink-and-you’ll-miss-her in the teaser, actually. So I got her in there as a Padawan.|archivedate=20230718195621}}</ref>}}
Tasi Lowa appeared in "[[Lost / Found]]," the first episode of the series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'',<ref name="Lost / Found" /> which aired on [[June 4]], [[2024]].<ref name="Announcement">{{SW|url=news/the-acolyte-teaser-poster|text=''The Acolyte'' Teaser Poster, Premiere Date Revealed}}</ref> She was portrayed by [[Thara Schöön]].<ref name="Lost / Found" /> Creatures effects artist [[Robert Skene]] worked on the mould for Lowa as part of [[Neal Scanlan]]'s team,<ref name="robskene-Instagram">{{Instagram|username=robskenefx|url=p/C9sKJa6oOFo|name=[[Robert Skene]]|date=2024-07-21|quote=Now that Acolyte has finished, here are just a few of the characters I was involved with bringing to life. Everything was a huge team effort with everyone at CFX, and it was a dream come true, getting to be a part of it. My contribution varied from character to character, including clay walling, matrix molds, drafting cores, processing 3d printed molds, molding prosthetics and more, working alongside the fantastic team in Moldshop under Kenny Wilson. #starwars #theacolyte #cfx #creaturecantina #moldmaking #mouldmaking|archivefile=File:RobertSkene-TasiLowa-Instagram.png}}</ref> while [[Martin Rezard]] sculpted the Padawan's prosthetics.<ref name="RezardEmail">{{EmailCite|email=File:MartinRezard-AcolyteEmail.png|creator=Martin Rezard|date=2025-10-05}}</ref> Lowa was first depicted in a trailer shown exclusively at [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]]<ref name="Celebration">{{CelebrationTrailer|''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''|Celebration Europe (2023)}}</ref> during the [[Lucasfilm]] Studio Showcase on [[April 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="Studio Showcase">{{SW|url=news/swce-2023-lucasfilm-studio-showcase|text=SWCE 2023: 11 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref> A trailer for the series released on [[May 4]], 2024 featured a voice line from the character, whose name was provided in the subtitles.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|6tzur6JrUEA|The Acolyte &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+}} {{Subtitles|YouTube}}</ref>

Showrunner [[Leslye Headland]] stated that a live-action Zygerrian was something she had wanted to include in the series<ref name="Collider" /> as a reference to expanded universe lore.<ref name="Interview">{{SW|url=news/leslye-headland-interview|text="Whatever You Think ''The Acolyte'' Is, It's Not": ''Star Wars'' Series Creator Leslye Headland Revels in the First Teaser Trailer}}</ref> The Zygerrian's appearance was achieved through practical effects, with Headland commenting that the makeup department had a lot of work as a result.<ref name="Collider" /> The StarWars.com episode guide for "Lost / Found" spelled the character's name as "Tasi Loa."<ref name="L/F Trivia">{{SW|url=lost-found-trivia-gallery-the-acolyte|text="Lost / Found" Trivia Gallery &#124; The Acolyte}} {{C|Slide 9}}</ref>

